+equality_checks:
+  - stage: after every block commit
+    compare: ledger rows vs commits (ledger-only and Regenerated-by commits excluded)
+    D: python3 .claude/skills/aider-scaffold/scripts/diff_ledger.py --check
+    CB: 'ci.yml: python .claude/skills/aider-scaffold/scripts/diff_ledger.py --check (fetch-depth 0)'
+    expected: '"0 commit(s) not in docs/diffs/INDEX.md" on both'
+  - stage: after annotating a block
+    compare: the three tree outputs vs a fresh render
+    D: tree_f.py … --check
+    CB: 'ci.yml: the same --check'
+    expected: '"tree_f --check: up to date" on both; a fresh clone renders byte-identical files'
+  - stage: after editing a surfaces YAML
+    compare: the Overview formulas' values vs the counts the builder prints
+    D: build_surfaces_xlsx.py --spec <yaml> --out <xlsx> --verify
+    CB: 'ci.yml: --out /tmp/surfaces.xlsx --verify'
+    expected: '"verify: OK"; Parallel + Conditional + Divergent == rows'
+  - stage: after adding or renaming a document
+    compare: the README Documents block vs the files under docs/ and notebooks/
+    D: update_readme_index.py … (write) then … --check
+    CB: 'ci.yml --check; the bot prints "No changes to commit" when the developer already refreshed it'
+    expected: '"README.md: unchanged" on all three'
+  - stage: after changing the generator
+    compare: committed workflow files vs the generator's current output
+    D: 'diff <(python3 .claude/skills/regen-workflow/scripts/new_regen_workflow.py --emit-reusable --print) .github/workflows/regenerate.yml'
+    CB: 'python -m pytest tests/test_regen_workflow.py -q (15 tests)'
+    expected: empty diff; 15 passed
+  - stage: before the push
+    compare: the fresh-clone replay vs the CI run
+    D: 'git clone … /tmp/replay; the whole "Verify before you push" block → REPLAY-OK'
+    CB: the verify job on the pushed head
+    expected: identical outcome — what passed in the replay passes in CI
+parity_meanings:
+  Parallel: same script, same arguments, same output on every surface (the README index)
+  Conditional: same result when the stated condition holds (same commit; the developer ran the regeneration before pushing; a PAT for the bot's commit to run CI)
+  Divergent: a stage only one surface performs (creating, reviewing, committing unattended); the trailer vocabulary and the checks make the surfaces agree afterwards
